��i<?php exit; ?>a:2:{s:7:"content";O:8:"stdClass":24:{s:2:"ID";i:5359;s:11:"post_author";s:1:"1";s:9:"post_date";s:19:"2026-04-01 09:57:02";s:13:"post_date_gmt";s:19:"2026-04-01 09:57:02";s:12:"post_content";s:1200:"<p>If you are planning a similar initiative, start with a thin end-to-end slice, instrument it in production, and expand scope only when telemetry supports the next bet.</p><h3 class="blog-details__h3">When to simplify the architecture</h3><figure class="blog-details__figure wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://nsc.test/wp-content/themes/NSC-Software/frontend/build/img/blog1.webp" alt="Performance Budgets for Web Applications — delivery context" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="675" /></figure><p>Performance budgets only work when product agrees what “fast enough” means for the business. Engineers alone cannot defend skipping a marketing pixel.</p><h2 class="blog-details__h2">How teams reduce risk while moving faster</h2><ul class="blog-details__list"><li>Budget third-party scripts separately</li><li>Test on mid-tier Android devices</li><li>Alert on regression, not only outages</li></ul><blockquote class="blog-details__blockquote"><p>Culture is what people do when nobody is watching the dashboard—how they escalate, how they admit uncertainty, and how they ship fixes.</p></blockquote><p>Real-user monitoring reveals markets on slow networks where lab tests lie.</p>";s:10:"post_title";s:40:"Performance Budgets for Web Applications";s:12:"post_excerpt";s:274:"Performance Budgets for Web Applications — Performance budgets only work when product agrees what “fast enough” means for the business. Engineers alone cannot defend skipping a marketing pixel. Real-user monitoring reveals markets on slow networks where lab tests lie.";s:11:"post_status";s:7:"publish";s:14:"comment_status";s:4:"open";s:11:"ping_status";s:4:"open";s:13:"post_password";s:0:"";s:9:"post_name";s:40:"performance-budgets-for-web-applications";s:7:"to_ping";s:0:"";s:6:"pinged";s:0